{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"mission":1,"hero":510},{"id":2,"agency":3,"agency_full":4,"sector":5,"dest":6,"color":7,"year":8,"status":9,"departure_date":10,"arrival_date":11,"transit_days":12,"vehicle":13,"payload":14,"delta_v":15,"data_quality":16,"credit":17,"links":18,"flight_data_quality":46,"fleet_refs":47,"flight":56,"name":494,"type":495,"first":496,"dispatch":497,"description":498,"events":499,"vehicle_stage":492,"flight_events":503},"galileo","NASA","National Aeronautics and Space Administration / Jet Propulsion Laboratory","gov","JUPITER","#0B3D91",1989,"FLOWN","1989-10-18","1995-12-07",2242,"Space Shuttle Atlantis + IUS","Galileo 探测器和大气进入探测器；发射质量 2560 kg；轨道器干质量 1880 kg","~14 km/s（估算）","partial","© NASA / JPL-Caltech — U.S. Government work, public domain. Cruise dates approximate Jupiter orbit insertion.",[19,23,27,30,34,37,40,43],{"l":20,"u":21,"t":22},"Galileo (spacecraft) — Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galileo_(spacecraft)","intro",{"l":24,"u":25,"t":26},"Galileo mission (NASA Solar System Exploration)","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/galileo/","core",{"l":28,"u":29,"t":26},"Galileo at JPL","https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/missions/galileo/",{"l":31,"u":32,"t":33},"NSSDCA catalog — Galileo Orbiter (1989-084B)","https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/nmc/spacecraft/display.action?id=1989-084B","deep",{"l":35,"u":36,"t":33},"Galileo Probe — atmospheric entry 1995-12-07 (NSSDCA)","https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/galileo.html",{"l":38,"u":39,"t":33},"Europa subsurface ocean evidence — Khurana et al. 1998, Nature 395","https://www.nature.com/articles/27394",{"l":41,"u":42,"t":33},"Ida + Dactyl — first asteroid moon (Belton et al. 1995, Nature 374)","https://www.nature.com/articles/374785a0",{"l":44,"u":45,"t":33},"End-of-mission Jupiter disposal 2003-09-21","https://solarsystem.nasa.gov/missions/galileo/in-depth/","sparse",[48,51,54],{"id":49,"role":50},"space-shuttle-stack","launcher",{"id":52,"role":53},"space-shuttle-orbiter","spacecraft",{"id":2,"role":55},"payload",{"events":57,"interplanetary_profile":101,"launch":491},[58,64,70,75,80,85,90,96],{"met_days":59,"type":60,"label":61,"description":62,"label_en":63},0,"launch","发射","STS-34从Atlantis航天飞机上部署Galileo和上面级。","Launch — STS-34 Atlantis / IUS",{"met_days":65,"type":66,"label":67,"description":68,"label_en":69},115,"flyby","金星——引力辅助","1990-02-10 距金星最近 16,000 km。VEEGA（金星-地球-地球引力辅助）方案由此开始：Galileo 从金星获取轨道能量，把远日点向外推。金星附近的热负荷超出了原设计规格；工程师在天线支杆上加装隔热层，后来正是它让高增益天线一直无法打开。","Venus — gravity assist",{"met_days":71,"type":66,"label":72,"description":73,"label_en":74},416,"地球第1次——引力辅助","1990-12-08 最近距离 960 km。两次地球飞掠中的第一次；两次合起来把轨道弯曲到足以抵达木星。Galileo 还传回了地球的光谱观测，作为生命探测方法的测试——像从远处一样分析我们自己的星球。","Earth #1 — gravity assist",{"met_days":76,"type":66,"label":77,"description":78,"label_en":79},741,"加斯普拉——首次遭遇小行星","1991-10-29 距小行星（951）加斯普拉最近 1,600 km。这是航天器首次拍到小行星的近距离图像。加斯普拉形状不规则，长约20 km，表明它是一个更大母体的碰撞碎片——印证了太阳系早期的碰撞历史。","Gaspra — first asteroid encounter",{"met_days":81,"type":66,"label":82,"description":83,"label_en":84},1147,"地球第2次——引力辅助","1992-12-08 最近距离 304 km——抵达木星所需的最后一次引力辅助。这次飞掠被用来再试一次展开高增益天线（它始终没有完全打开；整个任务期间都靠低增益天线工作，为此采取了大量数据压缩措施）。","Earth #2 — gravity assist",{"met_days":86,"type":66,"label":87,"description":88,"label_en":89},1410,"艾达与艾卫——第二次遭遇小行星","1993-08-28 距小行星（243）艾达最近 2,400 km。发现了艾达的微小卫星艾卫（直径1.4 km）——首个得到证实的双小行星系统。它证明小行星可以稳定地拥有卫星，改变了小行星动力学模型。","Ida + Dactyl — second asteroid encounter",{"met_days":91,"type":92,"label":93,"description":94,"label_en":95},2094,"arrival","探测器释放","Galileo 的大气探测器在抵达木星前5个月、即 1995-07-13 分离，沿一条略有不同、瞄准这颗巨行星大气的弹道轨道飞行。探测器没有推进系统——它的到达几何完全由分离机动决定。","Probe release",{"met_days":12,"type":97,"label":98,"description":99,"label_en":100},"edl_or_oi","木星轨道插入","主发动机点火使Galileo进入轨道；为期8年的卫星科学巡游开始。","Jupiter orbit insertion + probe descent",{"source_tier":102,"reference_frame":103,"departure_body":104,"arrival_body":105,"transfer_type":106,"waypoints_helio_au":107},"tier_1_5_hybrid","heliocentric_ecliptic_J2000","earth","jupiter","type1